n total 80: dine-in 16/80 = 0.20, takeout 20/80 = 0.25, delivery 44/80 = 0.55. Suburban locations have the larger delivery relative frequency (55% versus 25%). Dine-in is more common Downtown (45% versus 20%), and takeout is slightly more common Downtown (30% versus 25%).","explanation":null,"choices":[]}},{"content_key":"APSTATS-HDG-2026-GRAPH-024","source_version_id":"e75d8820-7e85-4bad-8056-98ba27af3b0b","source_content_hash":"703d24b3d6a3b7d034b56dbb2673f6e7","topic_code":"2.1","skill_code":"4.A","agreement":"unanimous","required_units":[2],"primary_unit":2,"difficulty":"Hard","proposed_content":{"stem":"Answer the following question. Submit one photograph showing your constructed graph and your written response together.","stimulus":"Employees were classified by department and preferred meeting format. Draw a mosaic plot so each department width is proportional to its total count and each vertical segment shows the conditional distribution of format preference within that department. Then compare the in-person preference proportions across departments and use the counts or mosaic areas to justify which department has the largest number of employees preferring in-person meetings.\n\n| Department | Video | Hybrid | In-person |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Sales | 10 | 10 | 50 |\n| Engineering | 50 | 25 | 15 |\n| Support | 35 | 25 | 55 |","prompt_json":{"stem":"Answer the following question. Submit one photograph showing your constructed graph and your written response together.","parts":[{"is_drawn":true,"part_key":"a","prompt_text":"Employees were classified by department and preferred meeting format. Draw a mosaic plot so each department width is proportional to its total count and each vertical segment shows the conditional distribution of format preference within that department. Then compare the in-person preference proportions across departments and use the counts or mosaic areas to justify which department has the largest number of employees preferring