0,"Hybrid":25,"In-person":15},{"Department":"Support","Video":35,"Hybrid":25,"In-person":55}],"evaluator_strategy":"human_shadow","capture_instruction":"Original research seed for hand-drawn AP Statistics graph-response grading. Do not expose criterion definitions to the person drawing the graph.","expected_graph_spec":{"x_axis":"department","y_axis":"conditional meeting-format proportion","representation":"mosaic plot"},"practice_modality":"supplemental_hand_drawn"},"canonical_answer_1":"Department widths are proportional to totals: Sales 70/275, Engineering 90/275, Support 115/275. Within each department, segment heights are its category counts divided by its total. Support has the largest in-person count: 55, compared with 50 for Sales and 15 for Engineering. In-person conditional proportions are Sales 50/70 ≈ 71.4%, Engineering 15/90 ≈ 16.7%, and Support 55/115 ≈ 47.8%. Sales has the largest conditional proportion, while Support has the largest count.","explanation":null,"choices":[]}},{"content_key":"APSTATS-HDG-2026-GRAPH-026","source_version_id":"38dc9a05-3a41-4ca8-bf28-040d62df283f","source_content_hash":"fcc492d7a9378b4337038424c6961089","topic_code":"2.1","skill_code":"4.A","agreement":"unanimous","required_units":[2],"primary_unit":2,"difficulty":"Hard","proposed_content":{"stem":"Answer the following question. Submit one photograph showing your constructed graph and your written response together.","stimulus":"Patients were classified by clinic location and appointment outcome. Draw a mosaic plot so each location's width is proportional to its total count and each vertical segment shows the conditional distribution of outcome within that location. Then compare the no-show proportions across locations and use the counts or mosaic areas to justify which location has the largest number of no-show appointments.\n\n| Location | Completed | Rescheduled | No-show |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| North clinic | 40 | 20 | 10 |\n| South clinic | 45 | 20 | 35 |\n