ion | Completed | Rescheduled | No-show |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| North clinic | 40 | 20 | 10 |\n| South clinic | 45 | 20 | 35 |\n| East clinic | 65 | 20 | 40 |","archetype":"mosaic_plot_interpretation","item_type":"frq","subtopics":["mosaic plot interpretation"],"hand_drawn":true,"content_key":"APSTATS-HDG-2026-GRAPH-026","rubric_type":"spatial","label_status":"ai_provisional_unapproved","rights_status":"independently_authored_synthetic_research_seed_unverified","stimulus_table":[{"Location":"North clinic","Completed":40,"Rescheduled":20,"No-show":10},{"Location":"South clinic","Completed":45,"Rescheduled":20,"No-show":35},{"Location":"East clinic","Completed":65,"Rescheduled":20,"No-show":40}],"evaluator_strategy":"human_shadow","capture_instruction":"Original research seed for hand-drawn AP Statistics graph-response grading. Do not expose criterion definitions to the person drawing the graph.","expected_graph_spec":{"x_axis":"clinic location","y_axis":"conditional outcome proportion","representation":"mosaic plot"},"practice_modality":"supplemental_hand_drawn"},"canonical_answer_1":"Location widths are proportional to totals: North 70/295, South 100/295, East 125/295. Within each location, segment heights are outcome counts divided by its total. East clinic has the largest no-show count: 40, compared with 35 for South and 10 for North. No-show conditional proportions are North 10/70 ≈ 14.3%, South 35/100 = 35%, and East 40/125 = 32%. South has the largest conditional proportion, while East has the largest count.","explanation":null,"choices":[]}},{"content_key":"APSTATS-HDG-2026-GRAPH-029","source_version_id":"270cc4d2-323c-43a9-9c2c-4277ffbea235","source_content_hash":"00a71d28e70cc20f98d9665acc06c34d","topic_code":"1.5","skill_code":"3.A","agreement":"deterministic_single_candidate","required_units":[1],"primary_unit":1,"difficulty":"Medium","proposed_content":{"stem":"Answer the following question. Submit one photograph showing your constructed graph 